Basically the same three reasons as I had for not going through with
it. But I think you could make an interesting IF game based on
nethack, although perhaps with limited replay value. At least the
IF-wumpus (Hunter, in darkness) and the centipede "clone" are
interesting or (slightly) thought provoking. ifquake less so, but IMO
it's worth playing for the descriptions of the wall, sky, floating
symbols and so on.

The problem with nethack is the sheer size and complexity of the game
engine, and that it has quite a long "story". You could railroad it
(cutting down the number of levels for instance), but then it wouldn't
really be nethack.. but seeing as someone did a great story about the
demon wandering round the dungeon and restoring after the visit of the
last adventurer, it might be possible to do something that isn't quite
nethack, but recognizable enough to make it worth playing.

(The story is here: http://www.audentes.ee/~virgo/Nethack/behind.txt
It's been posted here as well.)

